  "frontier_delta_g3gi": "UST.G3GI evaluates all253 scalar degree21 catalecticants against the exact18-dimensional P_delta kernel and selected18-dimensional primitive15 target at48 split fibers under two apolar conventions. Every one of the96 obstruction matrices has rank244 and the same nine-dimensional structural nullspace; every admissible scalar source induces rank zero. The complete scalar-kernel source class is excluded at the exact48-fiber tier, forcing a non-Hankel matrix-valued connection compiler.",
  "frontier_delta_g3gj": "UST.G3GJ compiles all18 canonical K6 directions into the selected corrected H02 source at the anchor. One42706x18 solve with zero residual emits a248x18 quotient matrix of rank18; the prior P_delta source is a nineteenth independent direction. This closes source injection, not the connection transform or primitive-plane identification. It also identifies a finite-field compatibility obligation: G3CQ values at GF11,gamma3 must be re-executed at GF21817,gamma5 or transported by a proved naturality map.",
  "frontier_delta_g3an_g3as": "UST.G3AO closes all 735 selected toric regularity systems; G3AP proves the selected ordinary top dimension is one; G3AM computes rank(D0)=33; G3AN executes all 22,072 added products and proves rank(E)=89, hence full selected finite response rank 122 and left nullity 126; G3AQ promotes the rank and unit minor to every same-residue characteristic-zero lift by the regular-polytope, Fitting and Nakayama chain; G3AS materializes the exact finite Nfull=L*N0 operator with shape 126x248 and rank 126. These response gates are closed with zero observed inputs and zero fitted parameters. G3AR is a strict nonpromotable same-source beta_C contract. The live frontier is now the B89 meridian, integral rank-1509 representative, certified 248-coordinate period/residue image, B103-to-G3AL frame transform and exact beta_C zero/nonzero decision. Modular nonzero is a rigorous no-go; modular zero is not endpoint closure.",
  "frontier_delta_g3at_g3au": "UST.G3AT proves that Gauss-Manin polarization reconstructs each adjoint vanishing-cycle covector from its primal vector, reducing the frozen three-path terminal transport from six to three rank-1509 ODEs, 9054 to 4527 scalar ODE unknowns. UST.G3AU proves the exact adjoint factorization r=N F S z and permits the 126 normal rows to be evaluated before all 248 beta rows. One separated coordinate closes a source-specific no-go; all 126 zero rows only select a survivor and do not weaken the full G3AR zero branch.",
  "frontier_delta_g3av": "UST.G3AV binds the committed B103 248+1013+248 residue basis and one-dimensional complementary top line to Mavlyutov's exact cup-product formula. It fixes the relative block weights -1/48, -1/36 and -1/48, proves that the common top-line integration scale cancels from every normalized A1 projector, and replaces a dense 1509x1509 polarization matrix by exactly 4527 characteristic-zero top-coefficient reductions for the three selected lines. The reductions and three nonzero self-pairing certificates remain to be executed after the primal transports finish.",
  "frontier_delta_g3aw": "UST.G3AW proves that the immediate finite-word and meridian-source problem does not require the 4527 full-row reductions. The six unordered pairings of the three transported lines form a symmetric 3x3 Gram matrix, and the G3AV weights combine each entry into one exact top reduction. If its three diagonal entries and determinant are nonzero, the ambient space splits into the Gram span and its fixed orthogonal complement, so three exact 3x3 reflections decide every generated word and source coefficient. The six reductions, nondegeneracy and integral normalization remain to be executed; full G3AV rows remain the fallback for a degenerate span or arbitrary ambient action.",
  "frontier_delta_g3ax": "UST.G3AX promotes the selected modular top functional to one uniquely normalized relative analytic functional on the full rank-123 graph-preserving residue ball, without fitting or selecting a member. The G3AP 39,725 minor omits exactly coordinate 28267 and has nonzero determinant modulo 101, so it remains a unit over the G3AI/G3AJ formal ball; G3AQ's free rank-one quotient extends the functional to all 92,979 relations. G3AD's fixed integer lift remains excluded. Relative existence, uniqueness and reduction compatibility are closed; one graph-ball member or the relative variables, its 39,726 values and the six G3AW contractions remain open.",
  "frontier_delta_g3ay": "UST.G3AY compiles the six G3AW scalar values and their full 123-direction first jet from one reusable unit-minor factorization. The adjoint formula reduces 124 forward right-hand-side solves to seven. It also proves a one-way finite unit screen: nonzero reduced Gram diagonals and determinant are units for every same-residue graph-ball lift, and a nonidentity reduced word cannot become identity in characteristic zero. Zero or identity modulo 101 does not promote. The screen requires exact DVR-reduced or independently finite common-frame vectors; numerical complex transport has no automatic finite reduction.",
  "frontier_delta_g3az": "UST.G3AZ makes the finite shortcut executable: a vendored hash-exact 1,509-coordinate B103 map, the certified 39,726-coordinate G3AP functional and the G3AW 3:4:3 formula now produce six finite Gram entries, determinant, reflections and an optional word decision. An end-to-end synthetic fixture passes and is independently transcript-replayed, but it is explicitly nonphysical. The source-admissibility theorem proves there is no automatic componentwise reduction of complex numerical transport into F_(101^6); production requires an exact DVR reduction, an independently exact finite common-frame transport, or direct characteristic-zero pairing evaluation.",
  "frontier_delta_g3ba": "UST.G3BA proves that three complete hash-bound regauged face covers with strict cross-cell interval separation force the selected A1 Gram matrix to be -2 I3, with determinant -8 and rank three. The resulting B96 three-node subsystem is independent and cannot detect the affine class. The compiler, source-hash binding and partial-audit nonpromotion rule are closed. In the frozen current audit, all 212,598 tested cross-cycle cell pairs are separated and none is ambiguous; every pair of partial cycle images also has at least one common scalar-coordinate separator. This is strong execution evidence but not yet the theorem. A passing complete-cover result retires these three nodes and requires an enlarged detecting subsystem.",
  "frontier_delta_g3bb": "UST.G3BB fixes the enlarged detector target without a new search. The selected oriented primitive chain Z_phys=(-T17+T26-T27+T28) tensor u_B is finite and closed, and the vendored B87/product-chain packets prove <h_Z,Z_phys>=1 and integral transgression index one. Poincare-Leray naturality therefore forces every correctly executed B89 transgression tau_PL(Z_phys) to have unit affine relation defect. The theorem selects the target and its sign; the finite meridian word, primitive rank-1509 coordinates, B103-to-G3AL binding, 248 period image and beta_C remain open.",
  "frontier_delta_g3bc": "UST.G3BC proves that any integrally normalized B89 meridian combination pairing one with the same h_Z source represents the same beta_C quotient class as the G3BB-selected transgression: the two duals differ by an integral vanishing cycle and their readouts differ by Pi_C(V_Z). B87 makes the ordered affine-residue ideal the unit ideal, so the first prefix with gcd one and deterministic extended-Euclid coefficients gives a canonical finite no-knob Bezout meridian. The compiler is exact and rejects GF(11)-only residues. Production integral affine residue values, the 248 selected B-sweep values and the used period columns remain open. Quotient equality does not authorize a G3AU normal-row substitution until N F annihilates the replacement period shift or the G3AR same-lift/common-frame contract is supplied.",
  "frontier_delta_g3bd": "UST.G3BD closes an exact two-sided direct Deligne quotient compiler. An exact integer membership R_B=sum n_j p_j in certified integral period columns proves beta_C=0 without requiring a complete period basis. Conversely, a hash-bound real dual-lattice character that is integral on the full period lattice or a certified saturated detecting quotient and whose R_B interval contains no integer proves beta_C nonzero; a full annihilator is the zero-period special case. This route decides the quotient directly and does not require G3AU period descent. The production B-sweep values, production integral period columns and one decision witness remain open.",
  "frontier_delta_g3be": "UST.G3BE proves that the selected delta-trivial Hartshorne-Serre normalization product cannot emit the ordinary rank-one visible GRR correction. Its base elliptic j is the exact nonintegral rational 132105539357000/288838009, so it is not CM and is not isogenous to the CM Fermat fiber. The product has no mixed algebraic line class; the required Gysin row forces a line square divisible by twelve, never -6. This does not exclude V3 or decide beta_C. The existing G3AC/G3AJ twisted graph-Prym construction remains primary; a support that simultaneously trivializes delta and carries the square-minus-six class is only an optional ordinary fallback.",
  "frontier_delta_g3bf": "UST.G3BF synthesizes B85's existing divisor-lattice 4Z cutset with the later exact Picard-rank-two, delta-orientation, B86 root and B87 saturation theorems: the algebraic K3-divisor product-tube pairing image is exactly 4Z inside the full eta9 tube image Z. The fixed root tube realizes pairing four and its Deligne quotient class is 4 beta_C. A nonzero root class therefore proves beta_C nonzero; a zero root class leaves possible four-torsion. The connected smooth eta9 locus permits transport to the fixed B89 marking, with path changes absorbed by integral periods. Unit generation of the finite ordered B89 residues guarantees a first odd integral residue, and that residue plus the root emits a canonical two-term pairing-one dual. Production now needs a hash-bound B89 root transport and readout first and, only on its zero branch, the first odd residue and its readout.",
  "frontier_delta_g3bg": "UST.G3BG proves that primitive projection sends the pairing-four root Rminus tensor u_B to the exact two-sparse rank-42 source (-e2+2f2) tensor u_B. Relative to four times the G3BB gamma dual, the exact source-kernel period shift is (-e2-2f2) tensor u_B. The root and optional G3AU shift inputs are therefore closed without a rank-1509 guess. Their integral transgression into the fixed B89 marking and the root's 248 readout remain open.",
  "frontier_delta_g3bh": "UST.G3BH proves an exact identity-marking no-go. A nonzero selected-residue restriction minor excludes Rminus times any projective target point throughout the same-residue G3AJ ball; two fixed-B89 pencil minors have Bezout gcd one; and the locked principal 33-direction graph slice has full root-incidence rank ten. The root tube remains valid, but no fixed-pencil or selected-endpoint direct-containment shortcut can transport it. A nonconstant smooth-moduli path with one-vector integral Gauss-Manin transport, or an equivalent fixed-B89 integral cycle construction, is now mandatory.",
  "frontier_delta_g3bi": "UST.G3BI constructs the previously missing start member exactly. The locked B67 integer Q(gamma) section is corrected by a canonical 19-term right inverse so that (A0-A1)|Rminus=0 at the Fermat point [1:-1:0]. Candidate zero requires no preserving displacement. At the good-reduction prime (11,gamma-3), all 3 basepoint and all 9 smoothness ideals are units; proper smooth good reduction promotes the displayed member to a smooth characteristic-zero eta9 complete intersection. The start-member clause is closed. A nonconstant smooth path to fixed B89, one-vector integral transport, terminal B89 marking and 248 readout remain open.",
  "frontier_delta_g3bj": "UST.G3BJ closes explicit path selection without enumerating the discriminant. On the algebraic correction pencil F_a=F_B89+a(F_G3BI-F_B89), the discriminant is a finite algebraic set because both endpoints are smooth. Every interior point of the upper transcendental arc a(t)=1-t+i*pi*t*(1-t) is transcendental, so the arc avoids every critical value for every Archimedean embedding. Ehresmann transport therefore defines the path-oriented integral class PT_G3BJ(z4). The path and abstract integral map are closed; terminal B89 coordinates or a meridian word and the 248 readout remain open.",
  "frontier_delta_g3bk": "UST.G3BK compiles the exact G3BI correction direction into the frozen eta9 operator charts. The H20 update is rank one over Q(gamma), with numerator [3261,1627,-611,-3170,-827,2917], and its sole algebraic chart pole is avoided by every interior G3BJ point; the same chart is a unit at both endpoints. The complete characteristic-zero H20-to-H11, H11-to-H02 and raw H02-to-pole6 derivative streams contain 4712, 19247 and 4712 entries. The good-reduction H20/H11/H02 updates have exact ranks 1, 982 and 6016, with matching-cover structural bounds 1, 1006 and 6037. Raw source-direction construction is closed.",
  "frontier_delta_g3bl": "UST.G3BL proves that the complete H11 G3BI endpoint presentation at (11,gamma-3) has rank 5438/5439. Restoring every one of the 1071 unused original-Jacobian columns does not repair it. This excludes that finite initializer presentation only and is not a characteristic-zero singularity claim.",
  "frontier_delta_g3bn": "UST.G3BN evaluates the exact selected G3BI endpoint H11 chart at (21817,gamma-5), obtaining determinant 276. The nonzero reduction proves that its determinant is a nonzero element of Z[gamma] and hence that this selected chart is invertible over Q(gamma). H11 endpoint chart existence is closed.",
  "frontier_delta_g3bo": "UST.G3BO solves all 248 exact H11 endpoint correction sources -3 P sC at all six roots modulo 21817. Every 5439 by 248 residual is zero and six-root interpolation is exact. The resulting power-basis tensor is one exact split-prime residue, not a Q(gamma) reconstruction.",
  "frontier_delta_g3bm": "UST.G3BM applies the selected targeted pole-six transform to all 248 G3BI correction sources at (11,gamma-3). The exact H02 first-return block has rank 248, determinant 7 and 56032 nonzero entries; the complete 42706 by 248 ambient return has 2778007 nonzero entries and retains the full lower-pole quotient support. The correction-specific first toric return is closed at the selected proof fiber.",
  "frontier_delta_g3bp": "UST.G3BP constructs the selected endpoint H11 chart at all 48 roots of eight completely split primes, and every determinant is nonzero. The seven-prime centered determinant candidate predicts 0/6 withheld coordinates and the eight-prime centered candidate fails the independent GF(11) endpoint screen, so the present modulus is provably insufficient. No centered CRT candidate is promoted; additional split primes and a proved height bound remain necessary.",
  "frontier_delta_g3bq": "UST.G3BQ feeds the G3BM ambient return through the exact original-Jacobian coordinate and Griffiths-Dwork divergence engine. All 248 correction sources return with zero residual through H02, H11 and H20. Their 1509 by 248 block has 340473 nonzero entries and rank 248. The complete correction-specific finite recursive return is closed at GF(11); characteristic-zero H11/H02 action, integral G3BJ continuation and terminal readout remain open.",
  "frontier_delta_g3br": "UST.G3BR rebuilds the selected 42706 by 42706 H02 endpoint chart from the exact characteristic-zero source columns and the 19-term G3BI update. Its determinant is 419 modulo 21817 at gamma=5. The nonzero reduction proves that this selected H02 endpoint chart is invertible over Q(gamma). Both H11 and H02 endpoint chart-existence clauses are now closed; their source-active inverse actions remain to be promoted.",
  "frontier_delta_g3bs": "UST.G3BS executes the complete 42706 by 1013 H02 inverse action on all exact -4 P sC source columns at (21817,gamma-5). The selected determinant is 419, the stored solution has 25446335 nonzero entries and its independently recomputed residual is zero. This closes one-root action execution only.",
  "frontier_delta_g3bt": "UST.G3BT extends the exact H02 source-active action to all six roots modulo 21817. The six endpoint determinants 419, 13232, 2913, 6224, 10294 and 7871 are nonzero; all six 42706 by 1013 inverse actions have zero residual; and the explicit 248 by 1013 by 6 quotient power-basis tensor has zero evaluation mismatches. The complete one-split-prime action is closed, while characteristic-zero reconstruction remains open.",
  "frontier_delta_g3bu": "UST.G3BU independently rebuilds all 48 corrected G3BI H02 endpoint charts over eight completely split primes. All residues are nonzero and interpolate exactly prime by prime, but every prefix holdout predicts 0 of 6 next-prime coefficients. The 125-bit centered CRT is therefore unstable and nonpromotable without a proved height bound or independent exact relation.",
  "frontier_delta_g3bv": "UST.G3BV rebuilds the corrected H02 endpoint at (11,3) and proves exact singularity with dependent selected column 42384, while the eight-prime centered CRT candidate evaluates to 2. This independently rejects the CRT alias and forbids transfer of the old GF(11) inverse; it does not contradict invertibility at the certified anchor (21817,5).",
  "frontier_delta_g3bw": "UST.G3BW removes the 248 quotient-identity rows and gives the exact corrected H02 DM decomposition: a 42458-square complement with 2325539 support entries, 17692 components and one 24767 core. The preliminary active update support has 15158 rows and 17676 columns. This is an exact execution reduction, not an evaluated characteristic-zero inverse.",
  "frontier_delta_g3bx": "UST.G3BX proves that the corrected endpoint and prior H02 reference have identical complement support, matching, DM maps, component order, core and active coordinate sets. The identity coordinate map is therefore an exact support-level intertwiner. Coefficients, determinant, anchor inverse and evaluated kernels do not transfer.",
  "frontier_delta_g3by": "UST.G3BY forms the complete uniform coefficient update H=[B1 B2 B3 B4 B5] on the 24767 core. Its 24767 by 88380 support has maximum matching 14419, and the selected 14419-square integer minor has determinant 10432 modulo 21817. Hence rank_Q(H)=14419 exactly. This is the minimal generic Woodbury dimension; further reduction must use a canonically mapped selected source-reachable subspace.",
  "frontier_delta_g3bz": "UST.G3BZ reconstructs the selected affine correction update Delta_C over Q(gamma). Its support has matching bound 6037, while exact number-field elimination finds five repeated components of rank 359 rather than 362. A 6022-square minor is nonzero modulo 21817, so rank_Q(gamma)(Delta_C)=6022 exactly. This is the exact selected-path update dimension, 8397 below the generic G3BY rank.",
  "frontier_delta_g3ca": "UST.G3CA hash-binds normalized P_delta and the G3BI deformation section, proves that u*v*P_delta*(t0*t1*t2)*C_section is an exact 100-term H02 class of Cox degree (9,1,2), and reduces it through the selected endpoint at all six roots modulo 21817 with zero residual. Every 248-coordinate quotient vector is dense and the complete 248 by 6 power-basis tensor interpolates exactly. This closes the selected endpoint source class and one-split-prime coordinates, not characteristic-zero reconstruction, flat rank-1509 continuation, spectral-frame binding, integral transport or beta_C.",
  "frontier_delta_g3cb": "UST.G3CB computes the complete B69 spectral-to-B103 H20 frame map at the common good-reduction fiber. The two 248-row lists overlap in 215 monomials and replace 33 each. Exact coordinate reduction has zero ambient residual; the frame has 1857 nonzeros, rank 248 and determinant 5 modulo 11, and its emitted inverse satisfies both identities. This proves characteristic-zero frame invertibility but does not reconstruct characteristic-zero entries or perform path transport.",
